
     You may specify the topics you wish to read directly on
the help command.  For example, to  read  information  about
using  the  keyboard, you can type "help intro keyboard" all
on a single line.

     If you leave off the word  'help',  then  the  computer
will  begin  scanning  for  subtopic  names starting at your
current location  within  in  the  topic  directory.     For
example,  if  you  are in the 'intro' topic already, you can
learn about the pause key by typing "keyboard pause".  
